{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund pay rise for NHS support workers in bands 2,3 and 4",
        "additional_details": "Phlebotomists start at pay band 2 which is 20p above the National Living Wage. Band 3 began at \u00a38.50 hourly 10 years ago. It\u2019s now \u00a313.16. Living Wage then was \u00a37.20 hourly and will rise to \u00a313.21 in 2027.\r\n \r\nWe believe for too many years now the \"agenda for change\" pay structure has not worked and that staff have been taking a real terms pay cut for years. There is so much experience amongst support workers that we are of the view this needs addressing. We are concerned that the pay is unfair across all bands but the pay for supports workers now does not represent the responsibility that they have.",
        "background": "Fund a pay rise for bands 2, 3 and 4, greater at least than the living wage rise, at band 2.",
